# Gauntlet domain knowledge

Every number, label and sentence on screen must survive a data center engineer looking at it. **NMC² judges run real facilities.** One wrong number (an inlet of 45 °C called "normal", a "server room" instead of a "data hall") loses them in 15 seconds.

## 1. The product

Old monitoring scripts go in. Verified new ones come out. Along the way, the process finds real problems in the hall that the old scripts were hiding.

- **Read:** Nemotron Super reads a legacy Nagios check (plugin + config) and writes a rule card. The real plugin is run to confirm each statement.
- **Find:** the old check is replayed over 21 days of recorded hall readings. Deterministic detectors find what it hid. Nemotron Nano writes each finding as two sentences and an action. Staff accept (work order) or dismiss.
- **Prove:** Nemotron Super writes Prometheus rules. The verifier runs the real plugin on every value the sensor can report and on generated timing traces. A one-shot translation fails; the Gauntlet loop passes. Certificate, human sign-off, tombstone.

Nemotron writes sentences and rules. Execution decides whether they're right.

## 2. The hall

- **Hall 1**, 4 rows **A–D**, 10 racks each (`A1`…`D10`, 40 racks).
- **Cold aisles** between A|B and C|D; **hot aisles** behind. Label them.
- **Cooling units:** one per row at the row end: `CU-A`…`CU-D`.
- **PDUs:** 2 per row, `PDU A-1` (racks 1–5), `PDU A-2` (racks 6–10).
- **D10 is decommissioned** (hatched, "Decom."). A legacy check still watches it.
- `D6`–`D8` are GPU racks (hotter, 20–35 kW).

## 3. Realistic numbers

| Quantity | Normal | Legacy warning | Legacy critical / danger |
|---|---|---|---|
| Rack inlet | 18–27 °C (typical 22–24) | > 27 °C | > 32 °C; throttle ≈ 35 °C; shutdown 40 °C |
| Outlet | inlet + 8–14 °C | — | — |
| Rack load | 4–12 kW (GPU 20–35) | — | — |
| PDU load | 30–65% | ≥ 80% | trip 100% |
| Cooling unit power | 18–24 kW running | — | — |
| Cooling per kW trend (CU-B) | flat | — | down 15% over 3 weeks = filter or refrigerant |

Legacy check config (use these exact values): `check_interval 1m`, `retry_interval 1m`, `max_check_attempts 3`, `notification_options w,u,c,r`, contact `rkowalski@` (left in 2023).

## 4. Vocabulary

| Use | Avoid |
|---|---|
| data hall, row, rack, cold aisle, hot aisle | server room, zone |
| cooling unit (CU-B); CRAC as secondary label only | AC |
| inlet temperature, outlet temperature | "temp" in headings |
| PDU, breaker | — |
| page, on-call, shift, handoff, work order | notification (in headings) |
| finding, accept, dismiss | anomaly, alert (for findings) |
| untrusted / faulty sensor | bad data |
| retire, parallel run, cutover, decommission, tombstone | rewrite, migrate code |
| certificate, counterexample, coverage, verified by execution | proven correct, 100% safe (without scope) |

