## 6. The six findings (exact copy)

Replay header: `Replayed check_rack_inlet over 21 days · 30,240 runs of the real plugin · it paged 214 times · 196 were the same false alarm`.

| # | Severity | Title | Sentences (Nemotron Nano) | Found by | Suggested action | Evidence chart |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Critical | B7 inlet sensor is faulty | "B7 reports 10 °C above its neighbours and above its own outlet, which is physically impossible. The rack is at about 26 °C; the sensor is wrong, not the rack." | neighbour-disagreement + inlet/outlet-gap detectors | Replace B7 inlet sensor; suppress paging on B7 until replaced | B7 reported (36 °C) vs neighbour estimate (26 °C) vs B7 outlet, 21 days |
| 2 | Warning | CU-B is losing cooling effectiveness | "CU-B still reports Running, but its cooling per kW has fallen 15% over three weeks. That pattern usually means a clogged filter or low refrigerant." | cooling-effectiveness-trend detector | Schedule filter change on CU-B; inspect refrigerant | Cooling per kW, 21 days, a slow slope down; legacy status flat `OK` |
| 3 | Watch | Row C pages every night at 02:00 | "A batch job warms row C by 2 °C at 02:00 and it recovers by 02:40. The old check paged 19 nights in a row and nobody acted." | periodic-false-alarm detector | Add a 30-minute hold during the batch window, or move the job | 21 nightly spikes, all under 30 °C |
| 4 | Info | D10 is still monitored | "D10 was decommissioned in March 2024 and is not in the inventory. This check watches an empty rack." | inventory cross-check | Retire `check_rack_inlet_d10` without replacement | Inventory row vs config line |
| 5 | Critical | Pages go to a mailbox nobody reads | "Every page from this check goes to rkowalski@, who is not on the on-call roster. Nobody has received these pages since 2023." | roster cross-check | Route to the on-call roster | Contact line vs roster |
| 6 | Warning | A4's sensor drops out | "A4's sensor failed to answer 3% of the time over three weeks. The old check returned UNKNOWN and paged, but the pages went to the dead mailbox." | missing-data detector | Check A4 sensor cabling; page on missing data to the roster | Timeout count per day |

Accepted in the demo: 1, 2, 5 (work orders #482, #483, #484). Dismissed: 3 ("Known"). 4 and 6 left for the judge to click.

